{"kind":"artifact","text":"Implementation report for explicit state@3 request authoring (request 65fa914a) at exact head bb65d89803533232f154aa7b53082838fa93d285 on request/explicit-request-authoring, two commits over current main 183211c3 (21341300c plus correction bb65d898), fifty-one changed paths, no ui or embed change, fulfilling my promise 07a271e5. This head corrects changes-requested 4d3375f2 by planner (evidence assert 45d2d2d4) on 21341300c, on the same promise per the adopted repair-continuity rule. Correction: (1) recovery before measurement: intent.DedupIdentity states the retry identity (target log, actor key, namespace, key) apart from a signed record and Signed.DedupKey calls it; for a state or reassign-if-unclaimed act carrying an idempotency key and a caller target_ref, buildActRequest first asks kernel.PriorAct for the act already accepted under that identity, rebuilds through the ordinary path on that act's target_repo and target_head with no ref read, and returns the rebuild only when it is byte for byte the accepted signed act; otherwise it falls through to a fresh filing that measures the ref and lets the kernel refuse the reused key. An identical retry therefore replays after its branch moved or was deleted. (2) Only the server-derived half is recovered: requestMeasurementOf returns target_repo and target_head, never target_ref, so a reused key naming a different branch rebuilds different bytes and is refused (idempotency key reused with different intent), never answered with the old request; the earlier restatePayloadTriple is gone. A fresh key against an unresolvable ref still refuses. The reference pages for gs state, MCP state, both reassign-if-unclaimed pages and architecture layer 7 now state this contract; the false claim that an accepted retry simply measures nothing is removed. New controls through the app boundary, the real CLI, MCP and resident POST /v0/act routes and the guarded replacement route: deleted-branch identical retry re