he named test and restored: caller target_repo/target_head refusal, branch-shape check, unresolvable-ref refusal, shared choice judgement and hold rule (TestCLIRequestRefusesBeforeAnyAppend); state@3 signing (TestCLIRequestStatesItsResult, schema reads state@2); reassign@1 schema, fold reading and own choice (TestCLIReassignmentStatesTheReplacementResult); accepted-act reproduction (TestCLIRequestMeasuresTheRefAtEachFiling, idempotency key reused with different intent); MCP and resident surfaces (TestMCPRequestStatesItsResult, TestResidentRequestStatesItsResult). I re-ran four of these whole-guard mutants myself in a separate detached worktree at this head with the same red lines. Gates at this exact head: gofmt clean, git diff --check clean, go vet clean, go build clean, go test -race -count=1 on internal/workroom, internal/app, internal/mergeplan, internal/service, internal/kernel, cmd/gs and cmd/gitseq-mcp all ok, go test -count=1 ./... exit 0 with all 35 packages ok, GOFLAGS=-count=1 make docs ok. Architecture: layers 3 (kernel, PriorAct), 4 (intent, DedupIdentity), 5 (workroom fold), 6 (app) and 7 (surfaces) change contract; docs/reference/architecture.md is updated in this head. Security: caller intent (target_ref, body, text, bases, attachments) is compared and never rewritten during replay; only server-derived measurement is recovered, from the same verified frontier Submit consults, under the caller's own key; refusals precede signing and append; a moved or deleted ref cannot separate a caller from the act they own, and cannot be used to obtain a different destination's request. Simplification: one shared resolver with an accepted-measurement parameter, no retry cache, no second state machine; restatePayloadTriple and requestTripleOf removed. Reviewer note: the recovery gate also fires for a release report carrying target_ref, costing one PriorAct scan; requestMeasurementOf returns nil for a report body so no second build occurs. Branch pushed to origin; worktree retained until merge.","body":{"commit":"bb65d89803533232f154aa7b53082838fa93d285","path":"internal/app/request_authoring.go"}}